### OAuth playground: send these from Rider (click ▶ next to each request)
###
### How to get a fresh, unused code + its code_verifier:
###   1. Put a breakpoint in TokenController.cs (first line of Token()).
###   2. Sign in from the Angular app. The debugger stops when Angular sends POST /connect/token.
###   3. In the browser: DevTools → Network → "token" → Payload. Copy `code` and `code_verifier` below.
###   4. Send the requests here while Angular's request is still paused.

@host = https://localhost:7208
@code = PASTE_CODE_HERE
@verifier = PASTE_CODE_VERIFIER_HERE


### 1) Discovery document: everything a client needs to know about this server
GET {{host}}/.well-known/openid-configuration


### 2) PKCE attack: right code, WRONG code_verifier → 400 invalid_grant
###    (The code is NOT burned, because PKCE is checked before the code is marked as used.)
POST {{host}}/connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=authorization_code&client_id=spa&redirect_uri=http://localhost:4200/callback&code={{code}}&code_verifier=AttackerDoesNotKnowTheRealVerifier_AttackerDoesNotKnowIt


### 3) Normal exchange: right code + right verifier → 200 with tokens (saved for the next requests)
POST {{host}}/connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=authorization_code&client_id=spa&redirect_uri=http://localhost:4200/callback&code={{code}}&code_verifier={{verifier}}

> {%
    client.global.set("access_token", response.body.access_token);
    client.global.set("refresh_token", response.body.refresh_token);
%}


### 4) Code reuse: send the SAME code again → 400 "Authorization code has already been used"
###    (Now resume the debugger: the Angular app's own request fails the same way.)
POST {{host}}/connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=authorization_code&client_id=spa&redirect_uri=http://localhost:4200/callback&code={{code}}&code_verifier={{verifier}}


### 5) Call a protected API with the access token → 200
GET {{host}}/connect/userinfo
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}


### 6) No token → 401
GET {{host}}/connect/userinfo


### 7) Tampered token: decode the access token on jwt.io, change "sub", paste the edited token here → 401
###    (The signature no longer matches the content.)
GET {{host}}/connect/userinfo
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_EDITED_TOKEN_HERE


### 8) Confidential client with a WRONG secret (HTTP Basic auth) → 401 invalid_client
POST {{host}}/connect/token
Authorization: Basic webapp WRONG_SECRET
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=refresh_token&refresh_token=anything


### 9) Public client asking for a grant it is not allowed to use → 400 unauthorized_client
POST {{host}}/connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials&client_id=spa&scope=openid
